Why fooproof armor (*in vanilla?)

- A +5 thoroughly burnt thoroughly rotted elven cloak is worth 5 AC.
- A +5 fireproof elven cloak is worth 6 AC.

A blank scroll can become any of a number of far more useful things,
including "enchant armor" so that all of your stuff can become either +4
or +5, depending on how lucky you get.

+4 DSM, +4 helm, +4 boots, +4 gloves, and +4 cloak give AC-19 even
if all the corrodable/rustable/burnable bits are "thorough".  This is
enough to ascend with and is the extreme worst-case, not the extreme
usual case. 

Using enchant armor scrolls for fooproofing is a mistake.

> Destroy weapon, if it works the same way, would serve the  
> same purpose and save scrolls or marker charges.

Rendering one scroll per game potentially worthwhile for Neutrals or 
Chaotics (Lawfuls will have Excalibur), and the rest blank paper.  I can 
think of smaller gameplay effects, but not many.

Also, off the top of my head, don't god-granted weapons come rustproof?
That would make exactly zero scrolls per game worthwhile.

